-- mu-erase: the erasure of an introduction at a mu family (M1 Stage J,
-- brief 3.1 and M1-PLAN.md:103).  The erased form is a KTag of the
-- family tid, the constructor index in declaration order and the erased
-- fields, and "zero", which takes no field, is a tag with no payload,
-- which is the tagged integer the sum already uses (SD-D5, SJ-D5).  The
-- file stood under erase-neg until Stage J landed the rows, where it
-- read the interim word of SG-D7 (brief 3.3).

mu N : Type 0 with
| zero : N
| succ : N -> N

def one : N := succ zero
